---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Customs | Aura Homes"
  description="Beautiful second-life rooms that bring people back to nature, one room at a time."
  descriptor="Customs"
>
  <main id="top">
    <section class="page-lead">
      <p class="story-kicker">Customs</p>
      <h1>Drawn for the site.</h1>
      <p class="story-lede">
        The room on a steel frame is the start. Some land asks for more: helical piles, a floor lit from beneath, a deck, or a few rooms planned as one stay. Those are drawn for the place, not picked from a catalogue.
      </p>
    </section>
    <div class="page-body">
      <h2>Glass</h2>
      <p>A structured deck, a net, and balconies with glass railings. The picture is the floor, the span, and the light under it. The longer page is <a href="/glass">the glass</a>.</p>
      <h2>A small resort</h2>
      <p>A few rooms in Canada or Costa Rica, built custom. Costa Rica does not have its photograph yet. Until it does, the snow is the reference, and the plan is the same: few rooms, built for the stay. See <a href="/resorts">the resorts</a>.</p>
      <p>The room you can ask about now is on <a href="/rooms">Rooms</a>. A custom site starts with a note on <a href="/contact">Contact</a>, or a name held at <a href="/pre-order">Pre-order</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
